{"diagnosis":"Candidate/bad runs overrepeat actions that fail to produce a new state, especially clicks, no-ops, and scrolling.","expected_mechanism":"State-change checking detects loops and forces a changed strategy or termination, reducing wasted operations and repeated failures. Cost: state-history bookkeeping and occasional premature pivots when legitimate repetition is required.","policy_text":"Before repeating an action or materially equivalent action, compare the latest observable state with the state before the previous attempt. If no relevant change occurred, do not retry unchanged: alter the target, method, or assumptions; gather new evidence; or stop and report the blocker. Permit repetition only with an explicit expected state change.","quantitative_evidence":[{"command":"go tool pprof -top agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"result:repeated has +1,261 operations of candidate/bad excess, accounting for 11.31% of the profile's displayed total magnitude; result:terminal is -92 and result:conclusion is -67, favoring base/good runs."},{"command":"go tool pprof -top -nodecount=20 -focus='result:repeated' agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"Within repeated-result operations, candidate/bad excess is concentrated in action:click (+639), action:noop (+356), and action:scroll (+277)."}]}
