{"diagnosis":"Repeated actions without progress are overrepresented in candidate/bad runs: 1,485 repeated operations versus 224 in base/good runs (6.63×), for a net bad excess of 1,261.","expected_mechanism":"A progress checkpoint prevents unchanged-state action loops by forcing reassessment and a materially different approach. Expected cost: small state-tracking and reasoning overhead, with occasional premature pivots when delayed progress is legitimate.","policy_text":"Before repeating an action on unchanged state, compare the latest observation with the prior one. If the previous attempt produced no material progress, do not retry unchanged: identify the failure cause, alter the target, parameters, tool, or strategy, or stop and report the blocker.","quantitative_evidence":[{"command":"go tool pprof -top -focus='result:repeated' -tagfocus='comparison_side=candidate' -nodecount=5 agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"Candidate/bad runs contain 1,485 repeated operations, including 679 repeated clicks and 441 repeated no-ops."},{"command":"go tool pprof -top -focus='result:repeated' -tagfocus='comparison_side=base' -nodecount=5 agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"Base/good runs contain 224 repeated operations in magnitude, including 40 repeated clicks and 85 repeated no-ops."},{"command":"go tool pprof -top -focus='result:repeated' -nodecount=30 agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"The differential profile reports +1,261 repeated operations, with positive excesses of +639 clicks, +356 no-ops, and +277 scrolls."}]}
