{"diagnosis":"Candidate/bad runs disproportionately repeat actions that have already failed to produce progress, especially clicks, no-ops/waits, and scrolling.","expected_mechanism":"Tracking action-outcome recurrence and requiring a changed approach interrupts unproductive loops, improving progress and completion. Cost: small state-tracking overhead and occasional premature abandonment of a repetition that might eventually succeed.","policy_text":"Track recent action, target, and observed outcome. If the same or materially equivalent attempt produces no new progress twice, do not repeat it unchanged: reassess the state, change the strategy or inputs, or stop and report the blocker. Repeat only when new evidence makes success more likely.","quantitative_evidence":[{"command":"go tool pprof -tags -focus='result:repeated' agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"Repeated-result operations total 1,485 on candidate/bad sides versus 224 on base/good sides: 6.63× as many and a signed excess of +1,261."},{"command":"go tool pprof -top -nodecount=30 -focus='result:repeated' agentreward-338-pairs-bad-minus-good.operations.pb.gz","finding":"The +1,261 repeated-operation excess includes +639 clicks, +356 no-ops, and +277 scrolls, showing recurrence across multiple action types rather than one isolated action."}]}
